From 9bd6ada17dd97381b9ec895057c6eb73d177a0e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 03:27:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix address/profile sync, add multi-address support,
 wishlist, and admin orders
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- account-dashboard.tsx: every Supabase write now checks .select() +
  error and surfaces a toast on failure instead of silently no-op'ing
  (likely root cause of the phone-not-syncing report). Default address
  is now actually editable (previously just static text). Addresses
  card supports add/edit/soft-delete/set-default for multiple saved
  addresses, not just a read-only list of the first two.
- New wishlist_items table + RLS (migration 011, also applied live).
  New WishlistProvider wired into the root layout; the heart icon on
  product cards now actually toggles wishlist state and prompts sign-in
  when signed out instead of doing nothing. Real Wishlist card added to
  the account page.
- checkout/page.tsx: removed the DEMO_USER mock entirely. Checkout now
  detects a real signed-in session on load and its inline sign-in does
  real supabase.auth.signInWithPassword (email-or-phone via a new
  resolveEmailOrPhone server action, mirroring the main login page).
  Signed-in customers with saved addresses get a picker instead of
  blank fields, with a manual-entry fallback.
- Found and fixed a real gap: /admin/customers had no nav at all (the
  nav only lived in products/layout.tsx, scoped to that one folder).
  Extracted a shared AdminShell and gave products/customers/email/
  orders their own thin layouts using it.
- New app/admin/orders section: list + detail pages with Mark as
  Paid/Shipped/Delivered/Cancel actions. Will show empty until the
  real checkout order-creation flow is built (separate, already-scoped
  work) — this just gives admin visibility once that lands.

Note: guest-order-to-account syncing (mentioned in an earlier chat) is
still pending — there's nothing to sync yet since checkout doesn't
write real orders to Supabase yet.

